 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” company for every rental home, but **Atlis Property Management** looks like a reasonable first company to interview: it serves West Palm Beach and advertises full-service management starting at 5%, with a $200 monthly minimum and no management fee while a unit is vacant. Those are the company’s own claims, so confirm the full fee schedule and contract terms directly.\n\nI’d compare it with **Kanga Property Management**, which is BBB-accredited and A+ rated, and at least one other local manager. Before choosing, ask each for:\n\n- A sample management agreement and every fee, including leasing, renewal, maintenance coordination, and cancellation\n- Recent references from owners of similar single-family homes\n- How they screen tenants, handle repairs, and report income and expenses\n- Their average time to lease and how they set rent\n\nThe best fit depends on your home, location, and whether you prioritize lower fees, hands-on service, or leasing speed.",
